>
  <p>A louvred pergola can let you adjust overhead shade without moving the furniture. The harder buying questions sit below the roof: whether the posts leave enough room for chairs, what carries the loads into the ground, where rainwater goes and who takes responsibility for the finished installation.</p>
  <p>Start with a measured layout and a written installation scope. A kit price, a nominal size and an impressive wind headline do not answer those questions. This is a research-based planning guide; AHC has not installed or tested the systems discussed here.</p>

